    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128-a3">

                <pb facs="0263" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg97"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">japanese official statement</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Peking</placeName> Gazette</hi>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-04">July 4,
                    1917</date>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>President Li, accompanied by two members of his staff, came at 9.30 on the
                    evening of July 2 to the residence of General Saito, Military Attaché of the
                    Japanese Legation, and asked protection for him. He arrived in a spontaneous
                    manner and without previous notice.</p>
                <p>Under these circumstances, the Imperial Japanese Legation, following
                    international usage, has decided to accord him the necessary protection and has
                    placed at his disposal a part of the military barracks.</p>
                <p>The Legation further declares that as long as President Li remains there, it will
                    not permit any political action on his part.</p>
            </div>
